    "image_with_text_kK4AKq": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_DMkPBE": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Common Adhesive Tapes Used in the Aerospace Industry",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_BqiPHj": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Aerospace adhesives are highly versatile and available from a variety of materials to meet particular needs. Some of the most common adhesive tapes used in aerospace applications include:</p><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/foil-tape\" title=\"Foil Tape\"><strong>Foil tapes</strong>.</a> Adhesive foil tapes provide excellent sealing for aerospace systems while providing protection from temperature fluctuations, moisture, and chemicals. Heat-resistant and corrosion-resistant properties coupled with electrical conductivity make foil tapes ideal for use in sensitive electronics and high-heat applications.<br/></li><li><a href=\"/pages/foam-tape\" title=\"Foam Tape\"><strong>Foam tapes</strong>.</a> Foam tapes provide added structure. With a variety of foam thicknesses and sizes, adhesive formulas, and backing materials, foam tapes provide sound dampening, insulation, cushioning, and sealing assistance.<br/></li><li><strong>Pressure-sensitive tapes</strong>. Engineered for quick, easy use, pressure-sensitive tapes are made using a pressure-sensitive adhesive that adheres under pressure. Since they don’t require additional curing steps or bonding materials, pressure-sensitive tapes are used to mount, fasten, and bond aerospace components securely and efficiently. They are also used to seal and cover specialized aerospace surfaces that cannot be painted or coated.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_DMkPBE",
        "text_BqiPHj"
      ],
      "disabled": true,
