    "image_with_text_wmALhC": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_zWTcDC": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Aerospace Industry"
          }
        },
        "heading_wqm7nG": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Key Aerospace Applications for Adhesive Tapes</strong>",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_EUR3yf": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Nearly every aspect of aerospace manufacturing and operation incorporates adhesive tapes to some degree. They are used to hold instrumentation and components in place throughout aircraft and to protect surfaces during painting, coating, and media blasting applications. They serve as electrical insulators, gaskets, and window masks, and are crucial for successful aircraft operation.</p><p>No matter what you need to fasten, seal, or insulate, NADCO has the right adhesive tape design and material for your needs. Aerospace applications that benefit from NADCO’s adhesive tapes include:</p><ul><li>Aircraft maintenance, repair, and operations (MRO)</li><li>Attachment, bonding, and holding of aircraft parts and equipment</li><li>Contamination prevention</li><li>Electrical insulation</li><li>Fastener retention</li><li>Long-term surface protection</li><li>Protection from chemicals, paint, and media blasting</li><li>Seating fabric, flooring, and carpet installation</li><li>Window masks</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "subheading_zWTcDC",
        "heading_wqm7nG",
        "text_EUR3yf"
      ],
